{title: Man Of Constant Sorrow}
{artist: Blackberry Smoke}
{key: A}
{# Источник: ручной перенос с UG. }

{comment: Intro}
[A]
[A]In constant [E]sorrow all through his [A]days

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]I am a man of constant [D]sorrow
I've seen [E]trouble all my [A]day.
I bid farewell to old Ken[D]tucky
The place where [E]I was born and [A]raised.
The place where [E]he was born and [A]raised

{comment: Verse 2}
[A]For six long years I've been in [D]trouble
No pleasures [E]here on earth I [A]found
For in this world I'm bound to [D]ramble
I have no [E]friends to help me [A]now.
He has no [E]friends to help him [A]now

{comment: Verse 3}
[A]It's fare thee well my old [D]lover
I never [E]expect to see you a[A]gain
For I'm bound to ride that northern [D]railroad
Perhaps I'll [E]die upon this [A]train.
Perhaps he'll [E]die upon this [A]train.

{comment: Verse 4}
[A]You can bury me in some deep [D]valley
For many [E]years where I may [A]lay
Then you may learn to love a[D]nother
While I am [E]sleeping in my [A]grave.
While he is [E]sleeping in his [A]grave.

{comment: Verse 5}
[A]Maybe your friends think I'm just a [D]stranger
My face you'll [E]never see no [A]more.
But there is one promise that is [D]given
I'll meet you [E]on God's golden [A]shore.
